WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.334
Russia's Victory

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.669
Day celebration this week

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.937
marking the Soviet Union's

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.005
defeat of Nazi

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:05.805
Germany

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:06.339
in World War

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.775
Two may not have seemed restrained

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.110
with its columns of troops

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.511
standing to attention

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.580
marching under the Tricolore.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.515
But it was a muted display.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.550
The Kremlin decided to forgo

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.753
the traditional flyover of warplanes

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.988
The parade featured only one tank.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.523
More than 20 cities

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.158
cancel their ceremonies

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:26.259
at a national march

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.728
honoring veterans were scrapped.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:29.662
Officials cited

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.797
security concerns

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.066
as the reason for the pared back events.

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.934
But President Vladimir Putin

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.603
might also have been unwilling

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.705
to ostentatiously celebrate

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.107
a 78 year old victory

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.409
when current news from

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.677
the Ukrainian front is bleak.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:45.512
Best estimates

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.181
say that as many as 200,000

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.083
Russian troops have been killed

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.017
or wounded.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.552
Many troops on the front line

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.254
lack proper supplies,

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.990
and the Ukrainian counteroffensive looms.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.159
Still, in his speech,

00:00:59.159 --> 00:00:59.893
Putin appeared

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.861
unbowed by these pressures,

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.896
casting himself

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.364
as the defender of a country

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.332
beset by the censure

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.635
of Western globalist elites.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:10.170
He may

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:10.770
want to start

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.972
worrying about his own elites

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.007
from the outside.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.275
It's easy to see Putin

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:15.542
as an

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.177
all powerful strongman

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.412
who rules Russia by decree

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.448
and has manipulated and mobilized

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:23.416
his people behind him.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.051
But in a fascinating interview

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.153
with Isaac Charlton of The New Yorker,

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.155
Tatiana Steno, via

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:29.823
a senior

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.024
fellow at the Carnegie

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.092
Russia Eurasia

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.960
Center, describes

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.029
a more vulnerable Putin.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:36.963
And that is in part

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.731
because Russian elites

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.500
have begun to grow disillusioned

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.835
with his leadership

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.203
and fear the outcome

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.138
of what they increasingly see

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.574
as an unwinnable war.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.408
Stunned, advised

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.909
Putin is a leader caught

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.511
between two sets of elites.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.345
On the one hand,

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.380
there is the progressive elite

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.615
made up of technocrats,

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.617
regional governors and senior officials

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.953
who view Putin as too extreme

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:00.520
and worry

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.921
about the effect of Western

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.790
economic sanctions.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:04.891
On the other hand,

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:05.859
there are what she calls

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:09.195
the patriots who see Putin as too soft.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.031
These voices are diffuse and plentiful,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.233
and they include men

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.101
such as Yevgeny Preclusion,

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:17.370
the head of the mercenary Wagner Group

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:17.770
as well.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.606
As the heads of the security services

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:22.142
and members of Putin's own party.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.377
These two groups align in their belief

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.313
that Putin is mishandling the war effort

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.916
a terrifying reality that

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:32.085
seems to emerge from this picture

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.319
is that Putin,

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.754
a man who started Europe's

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.890
biggest land war since World War Two.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:37.590
A man

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.825
whose policies are nothing

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:39.792
short of extreme

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.494
in the eyes of the world,

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.829
is far less radical

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.597
than the warmongering elite

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.566
in his own country.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.834
Son a view paints

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.736
a worrying portrait of governance

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.137
far from the sure footed,

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.306
centralized, vicious regime.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.108
Many in the West have come to nurture

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.910
in their imaginations

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.044
she tells The New Yorker

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.546
that arrests are carried out

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.014
by multiple agencies,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.016
sometimes without Putin's knowledge.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.318
Putin's own decisions appear confused,

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.320
based on which competing faction

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.289
influences him at the moment,

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:10.290
and Putin's view

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.325
can be at odds with his own agencies.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:13.693
For example,

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.062
Putin sees Prigozhin as a hero

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:18.164
even as the federal security services

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.800
and technocrats view him as a threat.

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:22.368
Putin also

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.169
faces more

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:24.737
severe economic pressures

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.472
than is widely believed

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.106
The Wall Street

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.408
Journal reported this week

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.076
that pollution data belies

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.277
the Kremlin's claim

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.245
that its industrial

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.980
production is recovering.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.682
Pollution in industrial regions

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.383
has dropped 6.2%

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.651
over the past year,

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:39.852
more than during the peak

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.254
of the pandemic.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.755
Russian official statistics

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.791
claim that annual industrial production

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.660
actually rose by 1.2% in March.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:50.129
And Jeff Sonnenfeld, a professor

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.497
at the Yale School of Management,

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.398
has pointed out

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:53.666
that Russia's energy

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:54.867
revenue is down

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.769
as a result of the G7 price

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.504
cap on Russian oil.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.107
Meanwhile, its budget deficit has soared.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.910
There is one silver lining for Putin.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.979
Whatever Russian elites may think of him,

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.748
he is still overwhelmingly popular

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:09.882
with the public.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.952
He has an enviable 83% approval rating,

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.520
according to the independent

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.055
Levada Center.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:16.756
Moreover,

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.091
the public does support

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.760
his ill considered war.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.363
But according to Stan, a via that support

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:25.965
just gives cover to increase repression.

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:27.767
It also keeps elites

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.535
who may privately oppose the war

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.237
from speaking out.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.505
The danger is not that

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.974
the Putin regime may collapse from within

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.109
she says.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:38.077
But that even under him,

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.245
it could transform

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.079
into something

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.482
monstrous, ruthless, inhumane.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.017
A reign of fear

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:45.918
as bad as the

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:48.454
Putin regime looks now in Russia.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:51.124
It could actually get worse.

